# wip356: the SONG screen is ONE page (K1 bar, K2 pattern, K3 repeat): SELECT has no second page to turn to, no "(1/2)" tag.
# FILL + SEQ brings the SONG screen back from any page (only in song mode). On the SONG screen, FILL (let go, nothing else used) asks DELETE BAR? and OCT+ deletes the bar on the cursor.
wait 300
# song mode with a 3-bar chain
key b10 down
tap SEQ
key b10 up
tap OCT+
tapkey w0
tapkey w1
tapkey w2
tap OCT+
expect songmode 1
expect view 5
expect songlen 3
expect curpage 1
# SELECT turned: still page 1 (there is no page 2)
turn SELECT 1 80
wait 200
expect curpage 1
turn SELECT -1 80
wait 200
expect curpage 1
shot songpage.png
# K3 = the repeat of the bar on the cursor (bits 5-7 of the bar's mute byte)
expect songbar1.5 0
turn K3 1 80
wait 200
expect songbar1.5 >31
# FILL + SEQ from another page: back to the SONG screen (and the SEQ page does not open)
tap EDIT
expect view 14
key b9 down
tap SEQ
key b9 up
wait 100
expect view 5
expect songmode 1
# a white key with FILL held adds the pattern, it does not delete
expect songlen 3
key b9 down
tapkey w5
key b9 up
wait 100
expect songlen 3
expect songbar1.1 6
# FILL alone (pressed and let go) deletes the bar on the cursor AT ONCE: no question (wip361)
expect songlen 3
key b9 down
key b9 up
wait 100
expect songask 0
expect songlen 2
# FILL + SEQ on the SONG screen itself: nothing is deleted
key b9 down
tap SEQ
key b9 up
wait 100
expect songlen 2
expect view 5
# the cursor on END (past the last bar): FILL deletes the last bar
turn K1 5 80
wait 200
key b9 down
key b9 up
wait 100
expect songlen 1
# FUNC + FILL is paste, not delete
key b10 down
key b9 down
key b9 up
key b10 up
wait 100
expect songlen 1
# out of song mode, FILL + SEQ only warns: the view stays
key b10 down
tap SEQ
key b10 up
tap OCT+
expect songmode 0
expect view 7
key b9 down
tap SEQ
key b9 up
wait 100
expect view 7
expect songmode 0
